---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Cookie Policy - TDEE Check"
  description="How TDEE Check uses cookies: what cookies are, which ones this site and Google advertising may set, and how to control or delete them."
  path="/cookie-policy/"
  crumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', path: '/' },
    { name: 'Cookie Policy', path: '/cookie-policy/' },
  ]}
>
  <article class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 sm:px-6 pt-10">
    <h1 class="text-4xl font-extrabold tracking-tight text-ink-900">Cookie policy</h1>
    <p class="mt-3 text-sm font-semibold text-ink-500">Last updated: October 2026</p>

    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">What cookies are</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      Cookies are small text files that a website asks your browser to store on your device. They let sites remember
      preferences, understand how pages are used, and, on sites supported by advertising, show and measure ads.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Cookies set by TDEE Check itself</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      TDEE Check is a static website and the calculators run entirely in your browser. The site itself does not set
      tracking cookies, does not require an account, and does not store your calculator entries on any server. Your
      inputs are used only to show your result on the page you are using.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Advertising cookies from Google</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      This site is supported by Google AdSense advertising. When ads are shown, Google and its partners may set and
      read cookies on your device to serve ads, limit how often you see the same ad, prevent fraud, and measure ad
      performance. Depending on your location and choices, ads may be personalized using those cookies. Google explains
      its own use of data on its page,
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="https://policies.google.com/technologies/ads" rel="noopener" target="_blank">How Google uses information from sites that use its services</a>.
    </p>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">How to control cookies</h2>
    <ul class="mt-3 space-y-2 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed list-disc pl-6">
      <li>Your browser settings let you block or delete cookies at any time. Blocking cookies will not break the calculators on this site.</li>
      <li>You can manage personalized advertising in your Google account ad settings, or opt out of personalized ads from many providers through industry opt-out pages for your region.</li>
      <li>Where a consent banner is shown on this site, your choice there controls whether advertising cookies are used.</li>
    </ul>
    <h2 class="mt-8 text-2xl font-extrabold text-ink-900">Changes to this policy</h2>
    <p class="mt-3 text-ink-700 leading-relaxed">
      If the way this site uses cookies changes, this page will be updated and the date at the top will change. For
      questions about cookies or privacy, see our <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/privacy-policy/">privacy policy</a> or
      <a class="font-bold text-brand-700 underline" href="/contact/">contact us</a>.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
